      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes the **Guarded Write Journal**, which is a mechanism that provides rollback capability for file writes in the guarded tool executor. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function**: Before overwriting any file, the guarded write path records that file\u0027s prior state into an in-memory journal \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a record that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n**Rollback mechanism**: If an agent run fails \u2014 whether due to exceeding a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or denied write attempts \u2014 the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order. It restores previous content for files that existed and deletes newly created files.\n\n**Purpose**: This gives each run **all-or-nothing semantics** for its writes without needing a database transaction. The journal itself acts as the transaction log, held only in the process\u0027s memory for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses the rollback path since it has no write capability at all \u2014 the journal type exists in the shared runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually write.",
